	(text "This is the power schematics of the project, USB C draws in 5V, \nwhich is then converted into 3.3V through the NCP1117 LDO. It can\nsink upto 1A of current, making it reliable even when running the \nscreen, LEDs, etc. all together! "
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 118.364 106.426 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.905 1.905)
			)
		)
		(uuid "2c19ccdd-2694-46bf-85fa-580227154240")
	)
	(text "Flash memory\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 34.798 124.714 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 3.81 3.81)
			)
		)
		(uuid "3d2b982b-e2d5-4358-b859-a91470079d62")
	)
	(text "This is the flash schematics for the MCU, the W25Q16VJSS IC\nis a 16Mb quad SPI IC, so it can transfer data, 4x as fast as \nSPI, which is ideal for flash memory"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 119.126 204.47 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.905 1.905)
			)
		)
		(uuid "6860d956-c90c-4e0e-aa3e-ce09d97d80a7")
	)
	(text "This is the MCU schematics for the macropad, I am using RP240 because\nof it's great documentation and beginner friendly! I also have added\nthe decoupling caps ( 8 power pins of 3.3v and 2 power pins of 1.1v ) \nand extra 1uF cap each to smooth out the current! Other than that, it \nuses a 12MHz crystal ( as mentioned in the datasheet and devboard guide )\nEverything here is pretty straightforward with labels describing use of\neach pints. "
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 354.838 145.288 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.905 1.905)
			)
		)
		(uuid "6b6b5b01-5584-4bee-aa80-c6fb19a7b2c9")
	)
	(text "LEDs"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 24.638 219.456 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 3.81 3.81)
			)
		)
		(uuid "dc40681e-ec38-4ba4-9aa3-265de892d777")
	)
